-- defect: non-exhaustive `case` — a 4-ctor union with only 2 arms (missing
--   `Amber` and `Off`). The covered arms `Red`/`Green` sort alphabetically
--   BEFORE the missing ones, and the union's declaration order (Red, Amber,
--   Green, Off) differs from both — so this locks that union resolution +
--   missing-ctor detection is order-independent (via the DefId `cr.type_` path
--   `union_members_by_def`, with the by-name `ctor_union` fallback behind it).
-- oracle: reject [E3001] (Sky exhaustiveness is a hard error — R1-D3)
-- context: F2 defensive gate. The `exhaustive.rs` `unknown union — lenient`
--   bail is unreachable for type-correct code (every matchable ctor is recorded
--   in the World's by-name + by-DefId maps). This fixture locks the resolution
--   path so a future change that regressed union resolution INTO that lenient
--   branch would resurface here as an ACCEPTED non-exhaustive program.
module Main exposing (main)

import Sky.Core.Prelude exposing (..)
import Std.Log exposing (println)

type Light = Red | Amber | Green | Off

name : Light -> String
name c =
    case c of
        Red -> "red"
        Green -> "green"

main =
    println (name Red)
